feat(attention): implement Grouped-Query Attention (GQA)

- Separate query heads from key-value heads (n_kv_head) to drastically reduce KV cache memory.
- Accelerate autoregressive decoding throughput for chord generation.

feat(ffn): add Sparse Mixture of Experts (MoE) SwiGLU FFN

- Replace static feedforward layers with a token routing mechanism.
- Distribute computation across multiple expert networks to specialize in diverse harmonic idioms (jazz, pop, blues).

refactor(embeddings): upgrade to high-base Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE)

- Increase frequency base (rope_base=500000.0) mirroring LLaMA 3 standards.
- Enhance long-range sequence context retention across extended musical forms.

perf(attention): integrate sliding window local attention

- Construct explicit causal masks to limit attention span to recent tokens.
- Lower compute complexity from quadratic to linear for long song structures.

fix(attention): introduce QK-LayerNorm for training stability

- Normalize queries and keys right before RoPE application.
- Stabilize gradient flow and prevent attention entropy collapse at scale.

feat(sampling): integrate repetition penalty and adaptive sampling

- Enhance sequence generation logic with dynamic penalty adjustments.
- Prevent repetitive harmonic loops during autoregressive chord prediction.
